# Images

Call `AppImages.initialize(this)` in Application.onCreate. It uses Coil's shared loader and caches.

```kotlin
AppImage(
    url = "https://example.com/avatar.jpg",
    shape = CircleShape,
    contentDescription = "User avatar",
    modifier = Modifier.size(48.dp),
    loading = { CircularProgressIndicator() },
    failure = { Text("Image unavailable") },
)
```

Use `placeholder = painterResource(...)` and `error = painterResource(...)` for local drawables.
Provide a fixed size/aspect ratio for predictable layout. No separate image downloader is installed.
For large lazy lists prefer Coil AsyncImage directly when subcomposition cost matters.
